/-!
# Lang's cyclic norm index inequality in ideal form

This module proves the lower bound half of Lang's norm index formula for a finite cyclic
extension `L / K` of number fields:

    `[L : K] ≤ [I(m) : P(m)·𝔑(m)]`

where `I(m) = idealCoprimeGroup K m` is the group of fractional ideals of `K` coprime to `(m)`,
`P(m) = principalRay K m` is the principal ray (principal ideals `(a)` with `a ≡ 1 mod* (m)` and
totally positive) and `𝔑(m) = normRay K L m` is the group generated by the relative norms of the
ideals of `L` coprime to `(m)`.  The modulus `m > 0` is assumed admissible (`IsAdmissible`, i.e.
the congruence units of level `m` are local norms at the primes dividing `(m)`) and divisible by
all the primes ramified in `L / K`.

The proof is the idèle-theoretic one: the ideal–idèle dictionary identifies
`I(m) ⧸ P(m)·𝔑(m)` with the quotient `𝕀_K ⧸ (Kˣ · W_m · N_{L/K} 𝕀_L)`, where `W_m` is the
congruence subgroup of the modulus; admissibility together with the ramification hypothesis gives
`W_m ⊆ N_{L/K} 𝕀_L`, so the index is exactly `[C_K : N_{L/K} C_L] = [L : K]` by the unconditional
cyclic norm index theorem `NK.GlobalCFTdeep.index_eq_finrank_of_isCyclic`.

The proof is carried out in the companion module
`Submission.NK.CFTLib.ArtinReciprocityIdeal.langCyclicRelIndex_proved` (the map `theta` from the
idèle group to `I(m)/(P(m)𝔑(m))` and the two inclusions `theta.ker ⊇ Kˣ·N 𝕀_L` and
`theta.ker ⊆ Kˣ·N 𝕀_L`); this module records the statement under its requested name.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false
set_option linter.unusedVariables false

open scoped NumberField nonZeroDivisors
open NumberField IsDedekindDomain

noncomputable section

namespace NK.CFTLib.ArtinReciprocityIdeal

theorem langCyclicRelIndex (K L : Type) [Field K] [NumberField K] [Field L] [NumberField L]
    [Algebra K L] [FiniteDimensional K L] [IsGalois K L] [IsCyclic (Gal(L/K))] (m : ℕ)
    (hm : 0 < m)
    (hram : ∀ p : NK.Chebotarev.PrimeIdeal K,
      ¬ NK.CFTLib.ArtinReciprocityIdeal.IsUnramified (K := K) (L := L) p →
      (m : NumberField.RingOfIntegers K) ∈ p.asIdeal)
    (hadm : NK.CFTLib.ArtinReciprocityIdeal.IsAdmissible K L m) :
    (NK.CFTLib.ArtinReciprocityIdeal.principalRay K m ⊔
        NK.CFTLib.ArtinReciprocityIdeal.normRay K L m) ≤
      NK.CFTLib.ArtinReciprocityIdeal.idealCoprimeGroup K m ∧
    Module.finrank K L ≤ (NK.CFTLib.ArtinReciprocityIdeal.principalRay K m ⊔
        NK.CFTLib.ArtinReciprocityIdeal.normRay K L m).relIndex
      (NK.CFTLib.ArtinReciprocityIdeal.idealCoprimeGroup K m) :=
  NK.CFTLib.ArtinReciprocityIdeal.langCyclicRelIndex_proved K L m hm hram hadm

end NK.CFTLib.ArtinReciprocityIdeal
